# L §5.7 example kinds and version, copied whole (the source bank_letter declared).  "x in brokerages over s"
# ranges over things alive on some day of s, subkinds included: broker (ordinary, from 2021-03-01) is alive on
# 2021-03-01 but not on any day to 2021-02-28.  "x in K on d tests membership on day d ... plain kinds with dated
# memberships included": wrapped from 2024-01-01.  "x in K tests membership of a kind whose memberships aren't
# dated (a base kind and its parents)": broker in brokerages.  (A membership test that ends an ask's body is
# written in parentheses, L §2.3 parse rule 4.)  "lifespan(k) is a record with .from and .to
# (never for an open end)": n7 lives 2021-01-04..2031-03-01, a span of days through 2031-03-01 (L §4.1).
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source bank_letter "a letter"

kind persons
kind accounts_pl: place PLN signed
kind lines: place PLN max 0
kind brokerages: place any min 0
kind ordinary: brokerages
kind ira: brokerages
kind wrapped
kind notes: unit
kind sales: event certain
  leg units: notes
  leg cash: PLN
  leg fee: PLN
  attr trade_ref: text

version opened
  cite bank_letter
  known 2019-05-01
  persons + [ola] lives 1990-02-01..
  accounts_pl + [konto] lives 2019-05-01..
  ordinary + [broker] lives 2021-03-01..
  wrapped + [broker] lives 2024-01-01..
  notes + [n7] lives 2021-01-04..2031-03-01

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

ask q1: count(x in brokerages over 2019-01-01 .. 2021-03-01), count(x in brokerages over 2019-01-01 .. 2021-02-28)
ask q2: broker in wrapped on 2023-12-31, broker in wrapped on 2024-01-01, broker in brokerages, (ola in persons)
ask q3: lifespan(n7).from, lifespan(n7).to, lifespan(ola).to
=== expect
q1: (1, 0)
  cut 2026-01-01
q2: (false, true, true, true)
  cut 2026-01-01
q3: (2021-01-04, 2031-03-01, never)
  cut 2026-01-01
